usages.usage:
LITERAL: " ### What it does
 Checks for files that are included as modules multiple times.

 ### Why is this bad?
 Loading a file as a module more than once causes it to be compiled
 multiple times, taking longer and putting duplicate content into the
 module tree.

 ### Example
 ```rust,ignore
 // lib.rs
 mod a;
 mod b;
 ```
 ```rust,ignore
 // a.rs
 #[path = "./b.rs"]
 mod b;
 ```

 Use instead:

 ```rust,ignore
 // lib.rs
 mod a;
 mod b;
 ```
 ```rust,ignore
 // a.rs
 use crate::b;
 ```
" in static DUPLICATE_MOD_INFO

