usages.usage:
LITERAL: " ### What it does
 Checks for blocks which are nested beyond a certain threshold.

 Note: Even though this lint is warn-by-default, it will only trigger if a maximum nesting level is defined in the clippy.toml file.

 ### Why is this bad?
 It can severely hinder readability.

 ### Example
 An example clippy.toml configuration:
 ```toml
 # clippy.toml
 excessive-nesting-threshold = 3
 ```
 ```rust,ignore
 // lib.rs
 pub mod a {
     pub struct X;
     impl X {
         pub fn run(&self) {
             if true {
                 // etc...
             }
         }
     }
 }
 ```
 Use instead:
 ```rust,ignore
 // a.rs
 fn private_run(x: &X) {
     if true {
         // etc...
     }
 }

 pub struct X;
 impl X {
     pub fn run(&self) {
         private_run(self);
     }
 }
 ```
 ```rust,ignore
 // lib.rs
 pub mod a;
 ```
" in static EXCESSIVE_NESTING_INFO

