LITERAL: " ### What it does
 Checks for `#[macro_use] use...`.

 ### Why is this bad?
 Since the Rust 2018 edition you can import
 macro's directly, this is considered idiomatic.

 ### Example
 ```rust,ignore
 #[macro_use]
 extern crate some_crate;

 fn main() {
     some_macro!();
 }
 ```

 Use instead:

 ```rust,ignore
 use some_crate::some_macro;

 fn main() {
     some_macro!();
 }
 ```
