usages.usage:
LITERAL: " ### What it does
 Checks for expressions of the form `if c { x = true } else { x = false }`
 (or vice versa) and suggest assigning the variable directly from the
 condition.

 ### Why is this bad?
 Redundant code.

 ### Example
 ```rust,ignore
 # fn must_keep(x: i32, y: i32) -> bool { x == y }
 # let x = 32; let y = 10;
 # let mut skip: bool;
 if must_keep(x, y) {
     skip = false;
 } else {
     skip = true;
 }
 ```
 Use instead:
 ```rust,ignore
 # fn must_keep(x: i32, y: i32) -> bool { x == y }
 # let x = 32; let y = 10;
 # let mut skip: bool;
 skip = !must_keep(x, y);
 ```
" in static NEEDLESS_BOOL_ASSIGN_INFO

