usages.usage:
LITERAL: " ### What it does
 Restricts the usage of `pub use ...`

 ### Why restrict this?
 A project may wish to limit `pub use` instances to prevent
 unintentional exports, or to encourage placing exported items directly in public modules.

 ### Example
 ```no_run
 pub mod outer {
     mod inner {
         pub struct Test {}
     }
     pub use inner::Test;
 }

 use outer::Test;
 ```
 Use instead:
 ```no_run
 pub mod outer {
     pub struct Test {}
 }

 use outer::Test;
 ```
" in static PUB_USE_INFO

