LITERAL: " ### What it does
 Checks for struct patterns that match against unit variant.

 ### Why is this bad?
 Struct pattern `{ }` or `{ .. }` is not needed for unit variant.

 ### Example
 ```no_run
 match Some(42) {
     Some(v) => v,
     None { .. } => 0,
 };
 // Or
 match Some(42) {
     Some(v) => v,
     None { } => 0,
 };
 ```
 Use instead:
 ```no_run
 match Some(42) {
     Some(v) => v,
     None => 0,
 };
 ```
" in static UNNEEDED_STRUCT_PATTERN_INFO

